1
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:43,580
Up Close with the Town! Downtown Cop

2
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,280
Are you here to film a TV program?

3
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:51,280
We received a request for
cooperation from a TV station.

4
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:57,480
They want to make a show about a police box and
its officers that still preserve the downtown charm.

5
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,920
This area has changed
quite a bit lately, though.

6
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,880
Downtown charm.

7
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:07,900
It's a chance to promote Katsushika
and improve our station's image.

8
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:11,120
I recommended the Kameari
Park-mae police box, so

9
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:12,600
Please take care of it.

10
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,500
Understood.

11
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,160
And one more thing.

12
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,360
for an officer who knows
the old downtown well,

13
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:20,400
could we ask him to serve
as a guide in the program?

14
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:23,240
Does that mean he'd appear on TV?

15
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,480
Of course.

16
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:28,200
When it comes to the Kameari Park police
box and someone born in the old downtown,

17
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:29,860
there's only one person.

18
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,300
If we make a blunder on
a nationwide broadcast,

19
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:39,080
it'll cause trouble for
the other officers too.

20
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:41,340
We must avoid that at all costs.

21
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,940
But Terai is from Hokkaido.

22
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:45,340
Reiko is from Kobe.

23
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:47,760
And Nakagawa was born in America.

24
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:53,700
Ohara, if he knows the old downtown well,
does it really matter where he's from?

25
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:54,760
I see.

26
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:58,020
Well said, Chief.

27
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:05,600
You want me to memorize
all of this in one night?

28
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,540
I know this is sudden,

29
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,780
but do it for the sake of the old downtown,
will you?

30
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:12,540
But if it's a downtown guide,

31
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:15,380
wouldn't a senior officer
be more suitable than me?

32
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,180
I know that already.

33
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:21,100
Asking Ryotsu, who knows what he might pull,

34
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:23,620
are we really risking
a major hit to our image

35
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:24,720
by going with someone serious

36
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:27,580
or a handsome young police officer?

37
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,100
We've thoroughly discussed it

38
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:31,160
with the station chief too.
This is our conclusion.

39
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:34,920
Well, you're also
stationed at this police box,

40
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,220
a lively downtown police officer.

41
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:38,820
It won't be staged, you know.

42
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,820
After all, it's a direct request
from the station chief himself.

43
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:44,740
Just sit back and complete the mission.

44
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,660
Senpai doesn't know about this

45
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,800
at all.

46
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:52,480
I got ahead of things and gave
Ryotsu the day off starting today.

47
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:55,600
He's probably out goofing
off somewhere by now.

48
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,300
Today's main event, the Kamiari Stakes.

49
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,820
They're off!

50
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,440
The horses are bunched up
together as they pass the far side.

51
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:05,020
Leading the way is Araragomencha!

52
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,300
Next up, Nanwokoumo

53
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,180
Now they round the fourth corner
and head into the straight!

54
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:36,840
Let's review.

55
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,520
Right.

56
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,360
This temple is

57
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:43,220
Daikyo-ji,
commonly known as Shibamata Taishakuten

58
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,160
Its features are

59
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:48,840
Its specialties are kusa-dango and Hyakkaen

60
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,860
Hyakkaen is in Mukojima.

61
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:53,660
Mukojima is Shobuen?

62
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:55,600
Shobuen is in Horikiri.

63
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:59,300
Right. Horikiri has Ohanachaya and Shobuen.

64
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:02,080
I haven't slept,
so my head's getting muddled.

65
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,540
So who's this girl?

66
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:08,980
Second son of Ao to Matsu Sushi, Okura-kun.

67
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:11,520
Correct! Then who's this one?

68
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:15,520
Ken'ichi-kun from the rice
cracker shop in Shibamata.

69
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,340
This one's Midori-chan from
the tempura shop in Kanamachi.

70
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:20,120
Ken'ichi-kun is this one.

71
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,160
No, no, no!

72
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:23,955
If it were Paris or Milan,

73
00:05:24,005 --> 00:05:27,240
I'd know even the waiters
at the back-street cafés.

74
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,060
But I only crammed all night,
so it's no wonder.

75
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:32,360
Well then, Nakagawa-san, please go ahead.

76
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,380
Ah, yes.

77
00:05:36,260 --> 00:05:37,140
Be confident.

78
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,120
Right, we're going live now.

79
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,820
5, 4, 3

80
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,940
D-damn it, you bloody fool!

81
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:49,720
Somehow it just doesn't feel right, does it?

82
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,400
Ha.

83
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:53,400
Tea sounds nice. Well then, please carry on.

84
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:55,240
W-we, we, we're...

85
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,600
the Hashizutsu-to-Tome
Gang of Date-Nishida-cho

86
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,400
I-I didn't do it, goddamn it!

87
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,980
S-sorry.

88
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:06,409
According to what I heard from Station
Chief Tomita of Katsushika Police Station,

89
00:06:06,459 --> 00:06:09,120
Nakagawa was born in Fukagawa,

90
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:13,101
His father is a torii craftsman, a trade
that has continued for ten generations.

91
00:06:13,151 --> 00:06:16,760
His mother is Haruyakko,
a former geisha from Yanagibashi.

92
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:22,320
So the older brother makes fireworks and the
younger brother is a rakugo storyteller, right?

93
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:25,280
Y-yes, that's right.

94
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:30,360
We were thrilled, since he's exactly
the kind of character this program needs,

95
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:33,820
but in person he looks like an
elite young man who was raised abroad.

96
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:35,380
They've seen right through us.

97
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:36,480
What do we do?

98
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:39,160
Actually...

99
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,580
I suppose the times have changed.

100
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:46,600
We'll add some staging on our end.
Is that all right?

101
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:50,280
I'll need you two to cooperate as well.

102
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,040
Us too.

103
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,260
Alright, let's give it a try!

104
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:03,980
This is just like Tora-san, isn't it?

105
00:07:03,980 --> 00:07:06,540
It's not like him, it's exactly him.

106
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:09,120
Yeah, yeah, it's starting to feel right.

107
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:14,140
Nakagawa's short trousers are also outrageously good,
a great look.

108
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,380
So, let's begin with Constable Nakagawa,
who has drifted back after six months,

109
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:21,780
with the scene where his two
colleagues warmly welcome him.

110
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:25,420
There's no officer who just drifts
back after six months like that.

111
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,780
You'll get fired, you know.

112
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,460
It's a burari stroll through the old downtown, so please go with
"burari."

113
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:32,620
Please go with "burari."

114
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,140
At this point,
we have no choice but to do as we're told.

115
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:37,360
That's right.

116
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,920
There, it's Kame-ari.

117
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:43,760
It's definitely Kame-ari.

118
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:48,000
Hey, workers,
still a bunch of idiots as usual?

119
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,060
Ro-chan

120
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:53,040
Hey, hey,
that's the full-day shift, you know.

121
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,700
The TV station?

122
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:57,920
Noren curtain, lanterns, camera, peace sign!

123
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,540
Okay, great!

124
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:02,740
Perfect.
You look so different, Nakagawa-san.

125
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,480
I'm over here.

126
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,120
Then who's this?

127
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:10,860
Ha-ha, I see.

128
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:13,520
Taking a few days to relax, he said...

129
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:17,240
I almost fell for the chief's sweet talk.

130
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:20,380
Ryo-chan,
weren't you supposed to go to the races?

131
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:24,060
It's your rare day off,
so why would you be at the police box?

132
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:26,500
A slight feeling of unease.

133
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:30,880
Nakagawa, raised in America,
posing as a cop from Inasena-shita Bridge...

134
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:34,100
I had a bad dream about
getting on a TV program.

135
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,440
Senior officer

136
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,660
Pass it along

137
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:38,680
Yes

138
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:43,180
I told the chief that a senior
officer would be better suited, too.

139
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:45,880
I said he's the right
man for the job, right?

140
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:51,040
We can't trust an important job to Ryo-san,
who might do anything unpredictable.

141
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:51,780
What?

142
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:58,280
That's right. If your daily work attitude were serious,
the chief would've asked Ryo-chan without hesitation.

143
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:03,420
Don't treat me like a kid. I can keep
my composure as an instructor, too.

144
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:04,240
Nice.

145
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:08,700
OK, cut! Please do that line again,
in the Beran-meichō style.

146
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,320
Beran-meichō

147
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,838
Damn it, you bloody idiot!

148
00:09:12,888 --> 00:09:15,620
Don't you go treating people like brats!

149
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,920
Like that, and... cue!

150
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:20,213
Nobody talks like that these days,

151
00:09:20,263 --> 00:09:22,900
except my damn old man, geez.

152
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,683
Damn it, quit your blabbering,

153
00:09:25,733 --> 00:09:29,440
who do you think you are, telling me to keep my
public and private lives separate, you bloody idiot!

154
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:31,211
Okay, cue!

155
00:09:31,261 --> 00:09:35,540
Kameari's the best!
Please, we'd love you to be our guide.

156
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:41,020
...we do ah... you won't find this anywhere else,
the real deal, straight from right here!

157
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,400
Keep me in mind, will ya!

158
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:52,300
I feel like I've become Tora-san!
The director seems to really like it.

159
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:59,380
Now, this is the scene where Ryo-san drifts back to
the police box and is warmly welcomed by his colleagues.

160
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:01,380
Please keep it friendly
and harmonious as usual.

161
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:05,500
It's hard to act "as usual" in this outfit.

162
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,900
Okay, let's start.

163
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,940
Haven't you lost a little weight?

164
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:13,800
Are you eating properly?

165
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:16,160
I'm the picture of health.

166
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:19,400
Healthy as ever, though I'm covered in
cat hair with cats all over the place.

167
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,080
I heard Ryo-san's back.

168
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:24,300
Didn't some beauty dump him again?

169
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:25,520
No, no.

170
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:29,840
That's because he was getting really
cozy with a beauty named Maria.

171
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,080
Turns out that "beauty" was a man!

172
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:36,400
Cut, OK! Great!

173
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,880
And now, Ryo-san,
who just had a huge fight with Uncle,

174
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:42,120
storms back out the door again.

175
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,220
Who's playing Uncle?

176
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:47,940
Ryo, what are you doing here?

177
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,620
You're off until tomorrow.

178
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:54,220
How dare you pass over me,
a shitamachi native,

179
00:10:55,520 --> 00:11:00,280
you've really done it, Chief! Of all of Katsushika,
when it comes to showing people around the shitamachi,

180
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:04,460
nobody beats me, you know.
It was the station chief's decision.

181
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:07,180
You have no right to nitpick me.

182
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:10,120
That's it.

183
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,440
Data OK. Great!

184
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:21,640
Next up, Ryo-san, who dashed out of the police box,
drifts in again, and this time an old lady appears.

185
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:30,640
Of course I'll show her the way. If I'm going to, I'd rather it be a gal!
Hey, don't forget you're on TV representing Katsushika station!

186
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:38,500
I'm joking, I'm joking. Since it's come to this, you're not going to do anything reckless.
I'll be there for all the filming, got it?

187
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:47,760
So you really want to be on TV too, Chief? Well, that's fine, Chief!
Let's work together for the image of Katsushika station.

188
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:51,300
Excuse me, where is Mr. Komine's house?

189
00:11:52,103 --> 00:11:55,660
Then just go straight and turn left.

190
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:59,400
Alright, then put that on and
say it again in Edo dialect.

191
00:11:59,875 --> 00:12:04,310
It's down this road, straight ahead
and turn left, that's how it is, see.

192
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,160
Berabō, you fool!

193
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:05,920
Thank you very much.

194
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:09,700
This is all just talk, geez.

195
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:11,180
Yes,

196
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:15,200
Next, please talk about the
environment around this police box.

197
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:21,360
The road flowing in front of this
police box is National Route 6.

198
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:24,820
Because it's the place where
the familiar Mito Kōmon is filmed,

199
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:27,600
it came to be called the Mito Kaidō.

200
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:31,800
Though the real Mito Kaidō
is the narrow road behind it.

201
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,120
This Route 6 is a newer road.

202
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,660
It was once even called Jūsanken Road.

203
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:40,300
Why Jūsanken Road? Well,

204
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,960
the road's width is exactly thirteen houses.

205
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:47,740
This is the famous mystery of Jūsanken Road,
a humble little tale.

206
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,840
And that concludes my tale.

207
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:50,620
OK

208
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:51,800
Splendid.

209
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:57,580
Don't you think he really came across as
a true shitamachi police officer, Chief?

210
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,000
Do you think so?

211
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:05,020
The way you cut Ryotsu off
just now was thrilling too.

212
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,740
Were you taking notes?

213
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:11,220
Yes, he had that dashing
shitamachi vibe oozing out.

214
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,020
Is that so? Ahaha.

215
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:17,420
Ryo-chan,
you're doing better than I expected.

216
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:21,200
After all,
he loves the shitamachi more than anyone.

217
00:13:21,660 --> 00:13:23,940
Yes, at this rate he'll be fine.

218
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,120
I hope so.

219
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:28,720
Somehow I feel like something's going wrong.

220
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:31,660
He gets to be on TV, so...
oh well, whatever.

221
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:58,660
Uuuuugghhh...

222
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,630
Chief, this is ridiculous.

223
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:02,700
Please say something.

224
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:05,700
Once you've taken it on,
you have to see it through to the end.

225
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:06,660
Chief!

226
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,460
This is your moment to shine, Ryo-san.

227
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,750
Carrying a mikoshi and
playing the manly hero,

228
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:15,620
dashing on patrol all the way to Shibamata,
just like that.

229
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:19,420
S-Shibamata!? Do you have any idea
how many kilometers that is from here!

230
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:22,300
Well, it's three kilometers
as the crow flies.

231
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:24,360
Are you trying to kill me!

232
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:28,560
Chief, at least help me carry it.

233
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:32,080
I can't. That lumbago from the
other day still hasn't healed.

234
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:35,120
Show me some Edo-kko spirit.

235
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:38,460
Chief!

236
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:44,340
Damn it! Now I'll show them the true spirit!

237
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,380
Yaaah!

238
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:51,640
Hey! Wasshoi! Wasshoi! Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

239
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:54,361
Huff and puff, huff and puff,

240
00:14:54,411 --> 00:15:17,740
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

241
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,620
Was your father also born in the shitamachi?

242
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:20,940
Well, that...

243
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:22,740
Never mind where he was born,

244
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,980
but he lives in Chiba now.

245
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:28,860
Okay, let's put in a dinner
scene with the two of them.

246
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,740
Get a shot of the shop sign.

247
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:33,120
Hehehehehehe!

248
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,860
Have you decided on your order?

249
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:36,900
Well then,

250
00:15:37,380 --> 00:15:38,660
one regular eel rice bowl,

251
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:41,660
one top-grade eel box with liver soup,

252
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:44,240
You're really treating all the staff?

253
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:44,800
Uh-huh.

254
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:48,620
Yo, yo, yo, I'll take the cheapest one here,

255
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:51,680
I see, so this is the
shitamachi spirit, is it?

256
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:55,140
I'm not falling for that trick,

257
00:15:55,190 --> 00:15:56,360
I see, I see.

258
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:59,760
Well, while we're at it,
add a cold sake, chilled.

259
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,934
Yes, five servings of top-grade,

260
00:16:01,984 --> 00:16:05,220
liver soup, and one more cold sake!

261
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:07,780
Hahaha.

262
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:21,320
It's always lively whenever I come here.

263
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:25,300
Thanks to you, I won't have any pocket
money until the end of the month!

264
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:28,120
Better than carrying
the mikoshi alone, right?

265
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,620
But I just don't get it.

266
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:32,100
Don't get what?

267
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:36,320
Looking back on everything
we've filmed so far,

268
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:42,000
with scenes like that,
can we really make a Katsushika PR program?

269
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,520
Of course we can't!

270
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:48,960
I always thought something
was off from the start.

271
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,700
So I was right after all.

272
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:57,440
At this rate, not just us but the whole station will
end up being laughed at across the nation, Chief.

273
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,100
That's a problem.

274
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:03,660
Station Chief Tomita is counting on this program for publicity,
after all.

275
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:07,860
I wouldn't be able to face my parents,
siblings, or ancestors either!

276
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,977
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

277
00:17:13,027 --> 00:17:16,223
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

278
00:17:16,273 --> 00:17:19,445
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

279
00:17:19,495 --> 00:17:22,716
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

280
00:17:22,766 --> 00:17:25,926
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

281
00:17:25,976 --> 00:17:29,185
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

282
00:17:29,235 --> 00:17:32,420
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

283
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:35,820
C-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

284
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:37,220
Let that person go.

285
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,460
Shut up already!

286
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,040
Then get out of the way, damn it!

287
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,060
Hey!

288
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:51,260
It stinks!

289
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:51,860
Are you hurt?

290
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:52,620
No, I'm not.

291
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:53,420
Wait, damn you!

292
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:57,100
Stop! Halt!

293
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:03,380
It's lucky we happened
to be filming right here.

294
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:04,760
I see.

295
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:08,820
What happened? We'll be right back,
so don't lose sight of the culprit!

296
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:10,540
Hey, Ryotsu!

297
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:11,880
Drop dead!

298
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:18,500
Ryo-san, I was just about to go call you.

299
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,580
Where's the cameraman?

300
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,060
Maybe he's in the bathroom?

301
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:23,240
Next, here.

302
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,700
This is a huge scoop,
it's more important than that!

303
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:29,700
Wait!

304
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:30,680
Should we wait?

305
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,940
But at this crucial moment,

306
00:18:34,940 --> 00:18:36,720
what on earth is Yōtsu doing?

307
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,200
Radio.

308
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:40,220
Sorry to keep you waiting. Radio.

309
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:43,300
What's that camera?

310
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:46,020
I came up with a brilliant idea
that kills two birds with one stone.

311
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,080
Brilliant idea.

312
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,100
I'll score a win within the show.

313
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,240
That way, we make that the main focus,

314
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,700
and the structure of the
program should change too.

315
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:56,600
Anyway, just chase the suspect!

316
00:18:56,600 --> 00:18:57,640
Forget about me.

317
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:58,560
Roger.

318
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:26,060
Can you not hear me?!

319
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:32,260
I'm a young punk called Sukeroku,
also known as Ryotsu of Kameari Kōen-mae.

320
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:33,460
Don't run!

321
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:38,620
Come closer and look up at my face!

322
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:40,380
What's that supposed to be?

323
00:19:40,770 --> 00:19:44,200
Don't play at being a gangster
when you don't even know Sukeroku!

324
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:48,840
Give back what you stole!

325
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:51,360
You still intend to resist?

326
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:52,960
You... whoa...

327
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,560
Um you bastard,

328
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,980
Heh, I took your food!

329
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:00,200
You're making a fool of me!

330
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:01,980
You bastard!

331
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:02,680
Hey, cut it out!

332
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,140
Whoa, no way!

333
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,620
Ryo-tsaa!

334
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:11,660
Ryo-tsaa!

335
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:14,900
He's a poisonous one. Hold him down tight!

336
00:20:15,220 --> 00:20:16,000
I know!

337
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:18,480
Let go! Let go of this!

338
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,500
I'm the one holding him up, me!

339
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:21,020
What?!

340
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:26,760
What's wrong, Ryotsu! I'm coming!

341
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,440
Hey, hey, hey, come on,
pull yourself together!

342
00:20:54,100 --> 00:20:55,460
Did you get it all on camera?

343
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:58,260
Yes, we'll definitely use this!

344
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:17,700
Thank you for your hard work.
Here, have this.

345
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:18,960
Th-thanks.

346
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:24,040
Ryo-san, Chief Ohara, I had
misunderstood the shitamachi until now.

347
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:26,440
Do you understand now?

348
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:29,880
See that? This is the spirit
of a shitamachi police officer!

349
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:35,600
Yes, I finally get it.
This will make a wonderful show.

350
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:36,780
Thank you very much.

351
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,800
No, thank you very much.

352
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:43,860
Looks like we managed
to save face after all.

353
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:45,340
That's a relief.

354
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:46,860
Wow, this is delicious!

355
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:51,820
Nyahahaha! My apologies, I got carried away!

356
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,500
Ryo-san!
I'm putting two cases of beer right here!

357
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,300
Large sea bream with the head, here you go!

358
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,340
Special nigiri, here you are!

359
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:04,820
Thanks! Just leave it there!

360
00:22:05,820 --> 00:22:08,660
Hehehe! I'll record it onto the latest DVD,

361
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:12,520
for generations to come,
I'll have my heroic deeds passed down!

362
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:14,660
Congratulations, Ryo-chan.

363
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:16,920
I hear you even arrested the robber

364
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:20,980
I was worried what would happen when
you went out with the Chief alone,

365
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:22,720
but it turned out well, didn't it?

366
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,020
This is a celebratory champagne.

367
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:27,460
You didn't have to go to such trouble.

368
00:22:27,460 --> 00:22:29,520
They say it's 300,000 yen a bottle.

369
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,780
You've got to be kidding!

370
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:31,920
Ryotsu!

371
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:35,220
The station chief himself is going
to give you words of praise, I hear.

372
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:37,340
It's kind of embarrassing, isn't it?

373
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:39,700
Komatsu, so this is what it's all about.

374
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:41,560
Well, I underestimated you.

375
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:43,200
Just Ryo-san...

376
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:46,880
It's all thanks to Chief Ohara!

377
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:48,460
Well, yeah.

378
00:22:48,460 --> 00:22:53,640
That director finally came to understand the shitamachi,
it seems.

379
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:57,100
I'm sure it'll do wonders for
Katsushika's PR and our company's image,

380
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:59,740
it should be a totally awesome program.

381
00:22:59,740 --> 00:23:03,460
I'm counting on it.
Let's watch from the front row.

382
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:05,740
It's about to start!

383
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:19,560
The Comedy Shitamachi Police Officer

384
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:25,340
And now,
today's Tuesday Wide Special is starting!

385
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:27,300
The Comedy Shitamachi Police Officer

386
00:23:27,300 --> 00:23:29,900
Does a police officer
like this really exist?

387
00:23:29,900 --> 00:23:31,460
Yes, he really does.

388
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:35,680
Laughs, laughs, and more laughs!

389
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:38,420
We'll bring you plenty
of shitamachi spirit too!

390
00:23:38,420 --> 00:23:39,120
60 minutes

391
00:23:40,540 --> 00:23:41,280
8 minutes

392
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,480
My apologies.

393
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:52,480
What is this, Ohara?

394
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:53,740
Well, that's...

395
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:55,380
Hey!

396
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:56,400
Ryota!

397
00:23:56,540 --> 00:23:58,640
It's not my fault!

398
00:23:58,640 --> 00:24:01,880
That director doesn't
understand anything at all!

399
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:20,420
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

400
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:27,120
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja

401
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:34,300
That strange feeling I had back then

402
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:39,520
So, on the arcade's tiles,

403
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:45,320
I walked only on the black ones.

404
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:53,600
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

405
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:57,600
Politicians with their self-important faces,

406
00:24:57,600 --> 00:25:00,900
and the aunties who
are a thorn in your side,

407
00:25:01,420 --> 00:25:06,580
turn at that corner, go on.

408
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:11,720
You can meet everyone, everyone!

409
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:16,340
Over there is Kameari,

410
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,660
surely there is Kameari.

411
00:25:21,080 --> 00:25:24,940
Everyone, come on over to our town!

412
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you.

413
00:25:31,020 --> 00:25:35,400
So you're the lowest scoundrel,
Kankichi Ryotsu, I've heard about?

414
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,680
Your face and your way of
talking are both vulgar.

415
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:39,860
Me?

416
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:42,900
I'm Remon Giboshi, Mato's little sister.

417
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:46,080
Next time: Super Kindergartener Remon.

418
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:47,100
Nice to meet you.

419
00:25:52,540 --> 00:25:52,900
Thank you.

